From: Nura GPU bring-up <gpu@nura.local>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos7580: add arm,mali-t720 to the GPU node

The Mali-T720 node only advertises the generic "arm,mali" compatible
string, which is what Samsung's kbase driver matches.  A Panfrost-class
driver binds on the model-specific "arm,mali-t720" (mainline panfrost's
dt_match entry, drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_drv.c:1167).

Adding the string as the *second* compatible keeps kbase's behaviour
exactly as it is today: of_match_table matching is per-string, and a
built-in kbase is registered and bound before any loadable GPU driver.
Nothing changes until kbase is disabled and a panfrost driver is built.

The other properties such a driver needs (clock names, power-domain
format) are not changed here: they require the kbase cutover and are
documented in parity/userspace/gpu/panfrost/design.md section 8.

Signed-off-by: Nura GPU bring-up <gpu@nura.local>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos7580.dtsi | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos7580.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos7580.dtsi
@@ -1064,7 +1064,9 @@
 	};
 
 	mali@0x11400000 {
-		compatible = "arm,mali";
+		/* "arm,mali" first: kbase keeps binding.  The second string
+		 * lets a Panfrost-class driver bind once kbase is disabled. */
+		compatible = "arm,mali", "arm,mali-t720";
 		reg = <0x0 0x11400000 0x0 0x5000>;
 		interrupts = <0 282 0>, <0 283 0>, <0 281 0>;
 		interrupt-names = "JOB", "MMU", "GPU";
